/*
# Window

A window inside a program — a pane with its own content, its own overlays and its own Tab
cycle. A menu, popover, dialog or sheet declared inside it opens over it: above its content
and past its edges, turning and scaling with it. A toast belongs to the whole program and
shows at the bottom of the App. Tab stays among the window's controls; F6 moves to the next
window, Shift-F6 back; a press inside it gives it the keyboard, back on the control that
last had focus there. A dialog or sheet open in it holds back presses aimed at this window
only — another window, or what lies behind, still takes them.

A window draws nothing of its own: its fill, stroke, shadow and rounding are yours. Its
children go into its `content` pane, which clips to its rounding; its overlays open in its
`layer`, above the content and unclipped. A title bar, resizing and stacking are the program's —
`raise()` brings a window to the front.

```declare
App [ width = 560, height = 300, fill = #E6E9EE,
    Window [ x = 40, y = 40, width = 240, height = 160, rotation = -4, cornerRadius = 10,
        fill = white, shadow = { shadow(0, 6, 20, 0x00000033) },
        more: Menu [ items = { [ ({ id: "rename", label: "Rename" }), ({ id: "copy", label: "Duplicate" }) ] } ],
        Text [ x = 16, y = 16, text = "A window" ],
        Button [ x = 16, y = 52, label = "Options", menu = { parent.more } ]
        ],
    Window [ x = 300, y = 70, width = 220, height = 140, cornerRadius = 10,
        fill = white, shadow = { shadow(0, 6, 20, 0x00000033) },
        TextInput [ x = 16, y = 16, width = 188 ],
        TextInput [ x = 16, y = 56, width = 188 ]
        ]
    ]
```

## overlays
The layer the overlays declared inside the window open in — its `layer`, read by them as
`provided("overlays")`.

## enter()
Gives the window the keyboard: focus goes back to the control that last had it inside the
window, else to the first. What a press inside the window does; a program's own way of
bringing a window to the front calls it too.

## holdsFocus()
Whether focus is inside the window now, in a program it hosts included.

## focusScope
`region`: Tab stays among the window's controls, and F6 moves between windows.

## onPointerDown
A press inside the window, on nothing that takes it, gives the window the keyboard.
*/

class Window [
    focusScope = region,
    defaultplacement = content,

    overlays: View? = { this.layer },

    holdsFocus() -> boolean { return Focus.holds(this) },

    enter() { if (!this.holdsFocus()) Focus.focusIn(this) },

    onPointerDown() { this.enter() },

    content: View [ width = 100%, height = 100%, clip = true, cornerRadius = { classroot.cornerRadius } ],

    // above the content and outside its clip: what opens inside the window
    // paints here, past its edges

    layer: View [ width = 100%, height = 100%, pointerEvents = "none" ]
    ]
